hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21407","He said: Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, saying: Humayd informed us from Anas from Ubadah that Ubayy ibn Kab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was sent down upon seven ahruf."
"21408","He said: Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, saying: Humayd informed us from Anas from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that Ubayy ibn Kab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me a verse, and he taught it to another with other than Ubayy's recitation, so I said: Who taught you it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. I said: By Allah, he taught it to me as such and such. Ubayy said: Nothing stirred in myself from Islam as stirred that day, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not teach me such and such a verse. He said: Yes. He said: This one claims you taught him such and such. He struck his hand upon my chest and that went away, and I found nothing of it afterwards. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril and Mikail, peace be upon them both, came to me, so Jibril said: Recite the Quran upon one harf, and Mikail said: Ask for more for him. He said: Recite it upon two ahruf. He said: Ask for more for him, until it reached seven ahruf. He said: Each is healing, sufficient."
"21409","Abdullah narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, saying: Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to me from Humayd from Anas that Ubayy said: Nothing scratched in my chest since I submitted except that I recited a verse, and he mentioned the hadith, and he did not mention Ubadah in it."
